ant species. Peas are eaten as a vegetable. The pea is native to the Mediterranean region and southwest Asia, and cultivated nearly worldwide."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-green-peas"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Green_peas"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked with","count":1,"groups":[["Indian cuisine","cuisine/indian-cuisine",[["Baingan bharta","dish/baingan-bharta"]]]]},{"h":"Often cooked with","links":[["Brinjal","ingredient/brinjal"],["Chili pepper","ingredient/chili-pepper"],["Cilantro","ingredient/cilantro"],["Coriander","ingredient/coriander"],["Cumin","ingredient/cumin"],["Garam masala","ingredient/garam-masala"],["Onion","ingredient/onion"],["Tomato","ingredient/tomato"]]}]},"dish/beijinho":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/beijinho","n":"Beijinho","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish from Brazilian cuisine","dot":"#94bd5c","intro":[["Beijinho, also known as branquinho (\"little white one\"), is a typical Brazilian birthday party candy prepared with condensed milk, grated desiccated coconut, rolled over caster sugar or grated coconut and frequently topped with a clove."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-beijinho"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Beijinho"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Brazilian cuisine","cuisine/brazilian-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":3,"links":[["Coconut","ingredient/coconut"],["Condensed milk","ingredient/condensed-milk"],["Sugar","ingredient/sugar"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"Olivia's Cuisine","ref":"site/oliviascuisine-com","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"oliviascuisine.com","note":"Brazilian-born Olivia Mesquita's blog, with a large section of Brazilian classics.","url":"https://oliviascuisine.com/","suggested":true},{"name":"Easy and Delish","ref":"site/easyanddelish-com","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"easyanddelish.com","note":"Brazilian recipe collection from a Brazi